  "title": "Ryan F Probable FDE 7212 NDE 7212",
  "date": "Summer 2003",
  "content": "I was driving on a dirt road in the 'middle of nowhere' Minnesota. I had my girlfriend at the time with me in the passenger seat. We noticed that she was going to be late for work if we didn't head back to the town. I don't remember the exact location anymore, but I remember driving about 75 mph so that my girlfriend could drive the car back to town, after dropping me off at home. As the car slid around the corner of a turn, I lost control and the car started rolling a couple times, going sideways into a field. All I can remember is floating above both my girlfriend and me as if watching a scene from a movie, rather than being involved in the accident. It was brief and as the car came to a halt in a nearby field, I was back in my body again, looking over at my girlfriend. I have been in other accidents and have not experienced this before. I was literally watching the scene unfold as if I were glued to the inside roof of the vehicle.",
